    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51233" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vīvĭfĭco</span></b> ,
			āvi, ātum, 1, v. a.
		vivificus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make alive</i>, <i>restore to
			life</i>, <i>quicken</i>, <i>vivify</i>
			(eccl. Lat.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mortalia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Apoth. 234</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. adv. Marc. 5, 9</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Val. 14 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aug. adv. Pel. 2, 10,
			33</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Paul. Nol. Carm. 26, 207</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 108, 11</span></i>.</div>
